# L1 (the graft build, cardm, no device): optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/build_k64j_lo.sh builds ~/opgraft-K64j-LO in the ttbuild container: K64j's exact source tree and patches (build_k64j.sh's
# staging, step for step) plus the ONE change of ag_link_offset.patch (a sub-device-1 all-gather connects to fabric link (link + QWEN_AG_LINK_OFFSET_SD1)). It never writes ~/opgraft-K64j and never
# overwrites an existing ~/opgraft-K64j-LO. Before it publishes anything it proves the result is K64j plus that change and nothing else: K64j alone, rebuilt in the same ttbuild, compared with the base
# binary (REPRODUCED = byte-identical, else a warning); every QWEN string of the base survives and the only new one is QWEN_AG_LINK_OFFSET_SD1; the exported symbols are the base's; _ttnn.so and
# every op directory are the base's; the manifest differs from the base's in one line. Then ttbuild is restored and rebuilt.
# READ: 'K64J_LO_TTNNCPP_SHA256=<sha>' and the line 'ok    REPRODUCED: K64j rebuilt alone ...' (the warning variant is acceptable only with the other checks green); the results hold the manifest, the QWEN-string
# and symbol lists and k64j-lo-build-summary.txt. STOP on any FAIL line: the next job needs the graft. Duration (estimate): 20 min (about three ninja runs of 30 to 60 s).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the separate-links run of the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own
# image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/build_k64j_lo.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=
